  "report_period": "Week 28 (5th Jul to 12th Jul 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Berge Bulk have committed their Newcastlemax \"Berge Bobotov\" 208/2021 Bohai, China (SS 07/2026, DD 11/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to Greek interests at USD 75 mill. For reference, the \"Trust Shanghai\" & \"Trust Qingdao\" 209/2021 SWS, China (SS/DD 04/2026 & SS/DD 02/2026, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) were committed a couple of months ago at excess USD 73 mill each. The Panamax \"Navios Taurus\" 76/2005 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 01/2025) of Navios Maritime Holdings was committed at USD 12 mill. Remind you that back in May, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Bravery\" 76/2004 Imabari, Japan (SS 06/2027, DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 12,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, Costamare committed their \"Oracle\" 58/2009 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 08/2024, BWTS fitted) to Vietnamese interests at USD 12,5 mill. Note that the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Gillingham\" 58/2010 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold a month ago at USD 13,9 mill. Moreover, the \"UM Elhanaya\" 56/2010 Qingshan, China (SS/DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed to Turkish interests at high USD 12 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Guo Tai Ping An\" 56/2011 Qingshan, China (SS/DD 12/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 14 mill. Maestro Shipping committed their Handysize \"Maestro Emerald\" 39/2020 Saiki, Japan (SS/DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted, OHBS) to Turkish interests at region USD 30 mill while the one-year-older \"Bamboo Star\" 37/2019 Minaminippon, Japan (SS/DD 12/2024, BWTS fitted, OHBS) was committed to clients of HMM at region USD 28 mill. Furthermore, the \"Cabrera\" 35/2011 Qidong, China (SS 11/2026, DD 12/2024, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1C, OHBS) of Falcon Maritime was committed at USD 14,6 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Dragonera\" 35/2011 Qidong, China (SS/DD 08/2026, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1C, OHBS) was sold back in March at USD 14 mill.",
    "tankers": "D'Amico committed their LR2 \"Mare Nostrum\" 110/2009 Mitsui, Japan (SS 02/2029, DD 06/2026, BWTS fitted) at region USD 44 mill. Remind you that the one-year-younger \"Alpine Confidence\" 107/2010 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 03/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold a month ago at USD 43,8 mill. Greek owners committed the MR2 \"Endless Summer\" 50/2010 Onomichi, Japan (SS/DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted) to clients of Gestioni Armatoriali at USD 30 mill. In addition, the one-year-older Korean built \"Zeze Start\" 50/2009 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 07/2024, BWTS fitted) was committed to Vietnamese interests at USD 27,5 mill. For comparison, the \"Gunmetal Jack\" 50/2009 Spp, Korea (SS 08/2029, DD 05/2027, BWTS fitted) was sold a month ago at region USD 28 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 15,000/17,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 10,000/13,000 pd. Australian trips into Japan were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. West African trips via North Coast South America into Continent were reported at the level of usd 12,000/13,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via US East Coast into India were fixed around usd 22,000/24,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 18,000/20,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 800K/1M. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 16,750 pd for 8/11 months employment basis delivery China.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of trips from China into India were fixed around usd 13,000/16,000 pd. Chinese trips into North Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Indonesian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Indian trips into China with salt were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "No fixture reported for this segment. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
